    5                 /       MUST BE ASSEMBLED WITH THE '/J' [PAL8 '/F'] OPTION SWITCH CLEAR.
    6   
    7                 /       P?S/8 ASCII TEXT-ORIENTED PAPER-TAPE UTILITY TO CONVERT P?S/8 TEXT FILES
    8                 /       FROM/TO ASCII PAPER-TAPES AS GENERALLY USED IN THE SO-CALLED "PAPER TAPE
    9                 /       OPERATING SYSTEM" [WHICH IS ACTUALLY JUST A BUNCH OF VAGUELY RELATED
   10                 /       STAND-ALONE UTILITIES THAT CAN BE USED TO DEVELOP SHORT PDP-8 PROGRAMS AT
   11                 /       GREAT EXPENSE OF TIME AND EFFORT ON A MACHINE WITHOUT A STORAGE DEVICE].
   12   
   13                 /       PTUTIL WAS WRITTEN PRIMARILY TO ENHANCE THE SIMULATED PDP-8 ENVIRONMENT
   14                 /       IMPLEMENTED IN THE P?S ADVANCED SIMH PACKAGE [PASP], AN ADVANCED
   15                 /       CONFIGURATION OF THE SIMH PDP-8 SIMULATOR.  BY TAKING ADVANTAGE OF SPECIFIC
   16                 /       FEATURES ONLY AVAILABLE WHEN RUNNING THE SIMH SIMULATOR FROM RECENT RELEASES
   17                 /       OF MICROSOFT WINDOWS, THE OVERALL IMPLEMENTATION ALLOWS REALISTIC PDP-8
   18                 /       PROGRAM DEVELOPMENT.  HOWEVER, P?S/8 [AS CURRENTLY DISTRIBUTED] LACKS AN
   19                 /       APPROPRIATE MECHANISM TO DIRECTLY INTERFACE WITH FILES OBTAINED FROM THE HOST
   20                 /       [WINDOWS] ENVIRONMENT.
   21   
   22                 /       PRIOR TO THE CREATION OF THE PTUTIL PROGRAM, THE PROCESS REQUIRED THE USE OF
   23                 /       OS/8 TO RECEIVE THE FILE UNDER DEVELOPMENT VIA THE PTR: HANDLER WHILE ENSURING
   24                 /       THE LIMITATIONS OF THIS PROCESS DID NOT INTERFERE WITH THE OUTCOME.  [NOTE:
   25                 /       THE OS/8 HANDLER IS FLAWED; PTUTIL IMPLEMENTS SUFFICIENT FEATURES TO PREVENT
   26                 /       ANALOGOUS PROBLEMS.]  BY PLACING THE OS/8 FILE ON APPROPRIATE DEVICES [SUCH AS
   27                 /       DTA1:], THE FILE CAN BE MIGRATED TO P?S/8 USING THE P?S/8 OS8CON [OS/8
   28                 /       CONVERSION] UTILITY.  FROM OS/8 IT IS THEN POSSIBLE TO BOOT TO P?S/8 IN THE
   29                 /       SAME SESSION, WHERE OS8CON CAN BE RUN AS PART OF A BATCH PROGRAM INCLUDING
   30                 /       CREATING AN ASSEMBLY LISTING OF THE FILE PASSED BACK TO THE HOST WINDOWS
   31                 /       ENVIRONMENT AS THE OUTPUT OF THE SIMULATED DEVICE 66 LINE PRINTER.  WITH THE
   32                 /       AVAILABILITY OF PTUTIL, OS/8 CAN BE COMPLETELY AVOIDED DURING THE DEVELOPMENT
   33                 /       PROCESS; P?S/8 BATCH CAN BE RUN AUTOMATICALLY IN AN INFINITE LOOP IF DESIRED
   34                 /       [SUCH AS WHEN MAKING FREQUENT EDIT/LISTING CYCLES] IN AN EXTENDED DEVELOPMENT
   35                 /       SESSION.  THE ENTIRE PROCESS CAN BE FULLY AUTOMATED OTHER THAN THE REQUIREMENT
   36                 /       OF PRESSING CONTROL-E TO EXIT THE SIMH ENVIRONMENT.  [NOTE: UNLIKE OS/8, P?S/8
   37                 /       RETAINS THE CURRENT DATE ACROSS REBOOTS.  MOREOVER, P?S/8 SUPPORTS THE TRUE
   38                 /       CURRENT DATE WHILE THE OS/8 DATE SUPPORT RAN OUT IN EITHER 1977 OR 2001
   39                 /       DEPENDING UPON WHETHER THE OS/8 USER CAN TOLERATE KNOWN KLUDGES THAT DO NOT
   40                 /       COMPLETELY FUNCTION.]
   41   
   42                 /       THUS, WITH THE AVAILABILITY OF PTUTIL, THE PASP ENCOURAGES THE USE OF HOST
   43                 /       EDITING AND FILE MAINTENANCE; THE SIMH SIMULATOR IS CALLED UP FOR BRIEF
   44                 /       SESSIONS FOR THE PURPOSE OF OBTAINING AN ASSEMBLY LISTING THROUGHOUT THE
   45                 /       DEVELOPMENT PROCESS.
   46   
   47                 /       THE PASP ENCOURAGES THE USE OF HOST EDITING AND FILE MAINTENANCE; THE SIMH
   48                 /       SIMULATOR IS CALLED UP FOR BRIEF SESSIONS FOR THE PURPOSE OF OBTAINING AN
   49                 /       ASSEMBLY LISTING DURING THE DEVELOPMENT PROCESS; THE PERMANENT COPIES OF
   50                 /       SOURCE CODE FILES ARE MAINTAINED IN THE HOST ENVIRONMENT [WINDOWS], NOT IN
   51                 /       EITHER P?S/8 OR OS/8.


/     P?S/8 ASCII PAPER-TAPE UTILITY  P?S PAL V08S    SAT  24-OCT-15  PAGE 2

   53                 /       IT IS NECESSARY TO FREELY INTERCHANGE SIMULATED PAPER-TAPE INPUT AND OUTPUT
   54                 /       BETWEEN THE SIMH ENVIRONMENT AND THE HOST ENVIRONMENT.  SINCE P?S/8 HAS
   55                 /       TRADITIONALLY SHUNNED PAPER-TAPE FOR ALL THE OBVIOUS REASONS GIVEN THE
   56                 /       PRESENCE OF STORAGE-BASED OPERATING SYSTEMS, IT DOES NOT PRESENTLY SUPPORT
   57                 /       A UTILITY OF THIS NATURE; PTUTIL CAN BE ADDED AS A TEMPORARY SYSTEM PROGRAM
   58                 /       [SEE BELOW] TO ALLOW THE DEVELOPMENT MECHANISM DESCRIBED ABOVE.
   59                 /       ANYONE WITH ACTUAL PDP-8 HARDWARE DEPENDING ON PAPER-TAPE DATA IS STRONGLY
   60                 /       ENCOURAGED TO ABANDON THIS APPROACH IF THEY HAVE SUFFICIENT HARDWARE TO
   61                 /       SUPPORT P?S/8.  SINCE MOST P?S/8 CONFIGURATIONS CAN RUN ON A 4K PDP-8 OR NEWER
   62                 /       MODEL [EXCEPT FOR THE PDP-8/S DUE TO INCOMPATIBILITY], IT IS RELATIVELY EASY
   63                 /       TO COMPLETELY LEAVE THE PAPER-TAPE ENVIRONMENT BEHIND.  [NOTE: PTUTIL ONLY
   64                 /       HANDLES ASCII TEXT PAPER-TAPE DATA; P?S/8 BIN CAN HANDLE ALL VARIANTS OF
   65                 /       BINARY PAPER-TAPE FORMAT INCLUDING BIN AND RIM FORMAT PAPER-TAPE INPUT AND
   66                 /       OUTPUT.]
   67   
   68                 /       RUNNING PTUTIL IN P?S/8 VERSION 8Z.
   69   
   70                 /       WHILE PTUTIL CAN BE MANUALLY ADDED TO THE P?S/8 SYSTEMS PROGRAM DIRECTORY, IT
   71                 /       WOULD TAKE CONSIDERABLE MANUAL EFFORT TO POSITION IT CLOSER TO THE BEGINNING
   72                 /       OF THE SYSTEM DEVICE WITHOUT A MAJOR REORGANIZATION OF THE EXISTING SYSTEM
   73                 /       PROGRAMS.  [FORTUNATELY, SUFFICIENT FREE SPACE WAS PROVIDED FOR ADDITION OF
   74                 /       SYSTEM PROGRAMS WHEN P?S/8 VERSION 8Z WAS FIRST RELEASED IN 1988.]  AS SUCH,
   75                 /       IT IS NOT RECOMMENDED THIS EXPEDIENT METHOD BE USED TO IMPLEMENT PTUTIL ON
   76                 /       THIS PARTICULAR P?S/8 RELEASE UNLESS RUNNING UNDER THE SIMH SIMULATOR. [NOTE:
   77                 /       FUTURE P?S/8 RELEASES WILL INCLUDE THE OPTION TO SUPPORT PTUTIL WITH PROPER
   78                 /       PROGRAM PLACEMENT.  THOSE KNOWLEDGEABLE OF P?S/8 SYSTEM PROGRAM DIRECTORY
   79                 /       PARTICULARS CAN ADD THE PROGRAM AT THE END OF THE CURRENTLY IMPLEMENTED
   80                 /       SYSTEM PROGRAMS; ONCE PTUTIL IS STABLE, A PROVISIONAL RE-RELEASE OF P?S/8
   81                 /       VERSION 8Z MAY BE PRODUCED.]
   82   
   83                 /       AS OF VERSION 8Y, P?S/8 INCLUDES THE ABILITY TO SUPPORT A TEMPORARY SYSTEM
   84                 /       PROGRAM:
   85   
   86                 /       .GET BPTUTL                             GET THE BINARY FILE[S] OF PTUTIL.
   87                 /       .R % [FILES AND COMMAND-LINE OPTIONS]   RUN THE PROGRAM AS % [OR $].
   88   
   89                 /       THE ONLY RESTRICTION PLACED ON A SYSTEM PROGRAM INITIATED BY THIS MECHANISM IS
   90                 /       THE REQUIREMENT OF A STARTING ADDRESS OF 00200 [WHICH IS THE USUAL PROGRAM
   91                 /       STARTING ADDRESS FOR MOST PDP-8 PROGRAMMING].  ANY COMBINATION OF COMMAND-LINE
   92                 /       OPTION SWITCHES, PASSED INPUT [OR OUTPUT] FILES OR USE OF THE =XXXX IS ALLOWED
   93                 /       IN A MANNER IDENTICAL TO PASSING PARAMETERS TO A PERMANENT SYSTEM PROGRAM.
   94   
   95                 /       [NOTE: IN LIGHT OF THIS MECHANISM, FUTURE RELEASES OF P?S/8 MAY REMOVE CERTAIN
   96                 /       SYSTEM PROGRAMS SUCH AS DEVICE FORMATTING PROGRAMS THAT ARE SELDOM USED.  AS
   97                 /       SUCH, THEY CAN BE PROVIDED AS BINARY FILES AND AN ACCOMPANYING BATCH FILE TO
   98                 /       PERFORM THE EQUIVALENT FUNCTION.  WHERE NECESSARY, THE PROGRAMS CAN BE PATCHED
   99                 /       TO ALLOW AN INTERNAL START AT 00200 TO CONFORM WITH THE R % OR $ MECHANISM.
  100                 /       USERS CAN MAINTAIN APPROPRIATE UTILITY FILES ON NON-SYSTEM LOGICAL UNITS FOR
  101                 /       INFREQUENT ACCESS ALLOWING GENERAL USAGE OF THE SYSTEM DEVICE AT GREATER
  102                 /       EFFICIENCY.]


