/     P?S/8 ASCII PAPER-TAPE UTILITY  P?S PAL V08S    SAT  24-OCT-15  PAGE 10

  327                 /       PAPER-TAPE INPUT FORMAT.
  328   
  329                 /       1)      LEADER SECTION.
  330   
  331                 /               WHILE OPTIONAL [BECAUSE TOTAL COMPLIANCE CANNOT BE FORCED], THIS IS
  332                 /               A SECTION OF PAPER-TAPE FRAMES WITH THE HIGH-BIT ONLY PUNCHED.  THE
  333                 /               LEADER SECTION CAN BE ANY CONVENIENT LENGTH [OR LENGTH ZERO].  PTUTIL
  334                 /               INITIALLY IS PLACED IN THE LEADER DETECTION MODE AS ALL LEADER FRAMES
  335                 /               ARE IGNORED.
  336   
  337                 /       2)      DATA SECTION.
  338   
  339                 /               THIS IS THE ACTIVE TEXTUAL DATA SECTION OF THE PAPER-TAPE.  FAILING TO
  340                 /               OBTAIN THIS SECTION WILL RESULT IN AN ERROR MESSAGE REGARDING THE LACK
  341                 /               OF INPUT DATA.  ALL DATA VALUES ARE ALLOWED EXCEPT A LEADER/TRAILER
  342                 /               FRAME [WHICH WOULD SIGNAL THE END OF THE DATA SECTION].  ALL PARITY
  343                 /               BITS ARE REMOVED BEFORE ANY FURTHER CHARACTER FILTERING FOR PROCESSING
  344                 /               INTO THE CONTENTS OF P?S/8 TEXTUAL OUTPUT FILES.
  345   
  346                 /       3)      TRAILER SECTION.
  347   
  348                 /               WHILE OPTIONAL [BECAUSE TOTAL COMPLIANCE CANNOT BE FORCED], THIS IS
  349                 /               GENERALLY A SECTION CONSISTING OF PAPER-TAPE FRAMES WITH ONLY THE
  350                 /               HIGH-BIT PUNCHED.  WHILE ANY CONVENIENT LENGTH MAY BE PRESENT, ONLY
  351                 /               THE FIRST TRAILER FRAME IS READ.  ASSUMING THE MULTIPLE INPUT TAPE
  352                 /               MODE ['/M' COMMAND-LINE OPTION SWITCH IS SET] IS IN EFFECT, THE
  353                 /               TRAILER WILL BE CONSIDERED THE LEADER SECTION DURING A
  354                 /               SUBSEQUENT READ OPERATION [UNLESS THE TAPE IS REPOSITIONED].
  355   
  356                 /       NOTE: IF THE DATA SECTION TERMINATES WITH THE CONTROL-Z CHARACTER, THE REST OF
  357                 /       THE DATA SECTION [IF ANY] AND THE ENTIRE TRAILER SECTION [IF ANY] ARE IGNORED.
  358                 /       IF THE MULTIPLE INPUT TAPE MODE IS IN EFFECT, THE USER MAY HAVE TO REPOSITION
  359                 /       THE TAPE IN THE READER TO AVOID JUNK [OR ALLOW THE JUNK CHARACTERS TO BE
  360                 /       PROCESSED WHICH MAY REQUIRE SUBSEQUENT MANUAL FILE EDITING].  [THE STANDARD
  361                 /       PAPER-TAPE FORMAT, WHICH IS CREATED BY PTUTIL WHEN PUNCHING PAPER-TAPE OUTPUT
  362                 /       DATA, CONSISTS OF A LEADER SECTION, A DATA SECTION TERMINATED BY CONTROL-Z AND
  363                 /       A TRAILER SECTION.  STANDARD FORMAT TAPES WILL ALWAYS BE READ CORRECTLY AND
  364                 /       COMPLETELY.  IF MULTIPLE STANDARD FORMAT TAPES ARE BEING READ, THE USER MUST
  365                 /       CHANGE PAPER-TAPES WHEN DIRECTED.]
  366   
  367                 /       THIS FORMAL DEFINITION OF PROPER PAPER-TAPE INPUT ALLOWS STANDARD TAPES TO BE
  368                 /       READ WITH EASE, YET ALLOWS NON-STANDARD INPUT TO BE READ, ALBEIT WITH SOME
  369                 /       NEED TO DO FOLLOW-UP EDITING AS REQUIRED.
  370   
  371                 /       FOR EXAMPLE, CERTAIN PAPER-TAPES WERE CREATED DURING FOCAL INPUT SESSIONS THAT
  372                 /       HAVE THE "*" PROMPT OF FOCAL STARTING EVERY LINE.  [THESE TAPES WERE GENERALLY
  373                 /       PRODUCED BY ENABLING THE PAPER-TAPE PUNCH ON TELETYPE MODEL 33 ASR OR 35 ASR
  374                 /       CONSOLE TERMINALS DURING THE ORIGINAL ENTRY OF THE FOCAL PROGRAM INTO THE
  375                 /       STANDALONE PAPER-TAPE RELEASE OF FOCAL, 1969 OR OTHER VERSIONS.]


/     P?S/8 ASCII PAPER-TAPE UTILITY  P?S PAL V08S    SAT  24-OCT-15  PAGE 11

  377                 /       AFTER USING PTUTIL TO TRANSFER THE PAPER-TAPE DATA TO P?S/8 TEXT FILES,
  378                 /       FOLLOW-UP EDITING CAN BE PERFORMED TO REMOVE THE "*" CHARACTERS.  [NOTE: AN
  379                 /       IMPERFECT SOLUTION TO THIS PROBLEM CAN BE ACHIEVED WITH THE KEYBOARD MONITOR
  380                 /       "CHANGE" COMMAND.  WHEN THE '/A' OPTION SWITCH IS USED, ALL OCCURRENCES OF THE
  381                 /       "*" CHARACTER CAN BE REMOVED; THIS WILL INCLUDE "*" CHARACTERS POTENTIALLY
  382                 /       USED IN THE BODY OF THE FOCAL STATEMENTS THAT MUST BE PRESERVED.  A COPY OF
  383                 /       THE FILE SHOULD BE LISTED OUT OR PRINTED WITH THE P?S/8 "PRINT" COMMAND TO
  384                 /       LOCATE THIS INCIDENTAL EXCESSIVE CHARACTER REMOVAL FOR MANUAL RESTORATION
  385                 /       AFTER ALL AUTOMATIC OPERATIONS HAVE CONCLUDED.]
  386   
  387                 /       NOTE: PAPER-TAPES CREATED BY LISTING THE FOCAL PROGRAM USING THE FOCAL "W"
  388                 /       COMMAND ARE UNAFFECTED BY THIS ANOMALY; THE STATEMENTS WILL BE PROPERLY STORED
  389                 /       AS INTENDED [FOCAL DOES NOT INCLUDE THE "*" PROMPT IN THE LISTING CREATED BY
  390                 /       THIS COMMAND].
  391   
  392                 /       LOW-SPEED READER CONSIDERATIONS.
  393   
  394                 /       WHEN THE LOW-SPEED PAPER-TAPE READER IS SELECTED [WHICH GENERALLY APPLIES ONLY
  395                 /       TO TELETYPE MODEL 33 ASR OR 35 ASR CONSOLE TERMINALS], CERTAIN RESTRICTIONS
  396                 /       WILL BE IN EFFECT DURING PAPER-TAPE READ OPERATIONS:
  397   
  398                 /       1) THE LOGICAL CONSOLE OVERLAY WILL NOT BE USED; ALL INPUT [AND OUTPUT] IS
  399                 /          DIRECTED TO THE PHYSICAL CONSOLE DEVICE.  [NOTE: IF APPLICABLE, THE
  400                 /          PAPER-TAPE READ SESSION WILL BE INITIATED BY PRESSING ANY KEY ON THE
  401                 /          LOGICAL CONSOLE KEYBOARD INPUT DEVICE.]
  402   
  403                 /       2) THE CONSOLE INPUT WILL BE SUBJECT TO A TIME-OUT.  FAILING TO OBTAIN CONSOLE
  404                 /          INPUT CHARACTERS WILL RESULT IN CLOSING THE INPUT DEVICE FOR DATA PURPOSES.
  405   
  406                 /       3) DUE TO HARDWARE RESTRICTIONS, IT WILL NOT BE POSSIBLE TO CHANGE THE
  407                 /          OPERATION OF THE PROGRAM WITH REGARD TO ANY OF THE NORMALLY SUPPORTED
  408                 /          CONTROL CHARACTER FUNCTIONS [<BRK>, CONTROL-A, CONTROL-B, CONTROL-C,
  409                 /          CONTROL-S/CONTROL-Q AND CONTROL-O]; ATTEMPTS TO USE KEYBOARD INPUT MAY
  410                 /          GARBLE THE INPUT DATA.

